
  Inglenook installer
  -------------------
  This is a root shell running from RAM. Nothing on any disk is changed until
  you do it yourself. The USB stick is only needed to copy the system image.

  1. Find the disk to install to (the stick shows TRAN=usb):

       lsblk -o NAME,SIZE,MODEL,TRAN,FSTYPE,LABEL

  2. The system image is on the stick, in /inglenook/ on its FAT32 partition
     (image.oci.tar.000, .001, ... and SHA256SUMS). Mount its partition
     (the vfat one in the lsblk output) read-only, for example:

       mount -o ro /dev/sda1 /mnt

  3. Partition, encrypt and install: the guided installer does not exist yet.

  4. When the image is copied, the stick can be pulled out.

  5. Reboot into the new system:  systemctl reboot

  Tools: gdisk sgdisk cryptsetup systemd-cryptenroll systemd-repart tpm2_*
         mkfs.* nvme skopeo curl git tar zstd lspci ip dig
  Nothing is saved on this stick; this shell resets on every boot.

